## Builder prompt

Copy this into a fresh IDE session at `/home/innerpixel/dev/sme-companion`:

```text
Read CLAUDE.md, ops/project.state.hybrid, ops/rules.constraints.hybrid, and ops/slice-1.homepage.hybrid.

You are the builder for slice-1. Coordinator (opus) has defined scope; you execute.

Tasks:
1. git init at repo root.
2. Scaffold SvelteKit (Svelte 5 + TypeScript + Tailwind) directly at the repo root. We will restructure into apps/web later when the FastAPI backend joins (slice-3); flat is fine for now.
3. Build / using blueprint §6 Page 1 structure and gtm-pack §3 messaging.
4. Build /demo using blueprint §6 Page 3 structure (the demo workflow page).
5. Build /app/inbox as a mock AI Inbox using static JSON. Source the 4 fully-written demo documents from romanian_sme_ai_companion_project_control_pack.md §23.3. Mock the analysis output (classification, summary, extracted fields, suggested action, urgency) using the "Expected extraction" / "Expected summary" blocks already written in that section.
6. Visual style: dark-gray palette per ops/rules.constraints.hybrid §Visual. Calm. Anti-hype.
7. Minimal README pointing at the docs and ops/.
8. When done:
   - git commit with a clear message
   - append ONE line to ops/slice-1.homepage.hybrid PATCHLOG (timestamp · model · summary)
   - update STATE in slice-1 frontmatter from "forming" to "stable"
   - append ONE line to ops/project.state.hybrid PATCHLOG and update §Now (current → next slice)

Confirm the plan in 3 lines, then start with step 1.

Out of scope: backend, real AI, upload, auth, Ask My Company, Draft Reply, the 12 missing demo docs.

If you hit a blocker: stop, append a line to slice-1 OPEN EDGES, commit what you have, report back. Do not improvise scope.
```

